lues that no passage chooses, and the window then rules out any transaction outside it."},{"clause":"dispute only the ones they deny","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 step 6: 'If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute'. The customer's denial is what identifies a transaction as unauthorized."},{"clause":"card_present_fraud / card_not_present_fraud by channel, atm_withdrawal, pin_purchase","kind":"derived","source":"The doc 031 fraud split by channel, plus the doc 031 transaction_type definitions."}],"rewrite":{"id":"from_pin_lock_handoff","by":"model","do":"This job can start from the PIN lock investigation: a card that cannot be unlocked, with successful transactions in the suspicious period that the customer confirms were not theirs. Doc 041 names the suspicious period but does not bound it, so do not rule any transaction in or out by date. Show the customer the successful transactions on the card from the earliest declined PIN attempt (type 'atm_withdrawal_declined' or 'pos_declined') in get_transactions that led to the lock up to the current time from get_time, and ask which of them were not theirs. Also ask whether any other recent successful transaction on the card was not theirs. Dispute only the ones they deny. Reuse the verification and the records already read, and continue at get_dispute_status.
