- offer the protocol's options: card closure and replacement (recommended if fraud is suspected), a transfer to the security team for investigation, or a PIN reset.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions","get_time"],"after":[],"if":"the job would start from the PIN lock investigation but the customer denies no successful transaction on the card","quote":"If no unauthorized transactions: Explain the security concern and offer options:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041","basis":[{"clause":"no unauthorized: explain and offer options","quote":"If no unauthorized transactions: Explain the security concern and offer options:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"clause":"check for successful unauthorized transactions","quote":"Check transaction history for any successful unauthorized transactions during the suspicious period.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"clause":"declined attempt types","quote":"Review the declined transaction history (transactions with type 'atm_withdrawal_declined' or 'pos_declined')","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"clause":"which transactions the customer denies","source":"none","why":"Doc 041 gives the suspicious period no bounds, so the customer is asked about the shown window and any other recent successful transaction instead of the step ruling on dates."}]}},{"step":"pin_lock_each_withdrawal","verdict":"rewrite","why":"Filing one dispute per transaction_id is derived, but the fixed suspicious-period window is unsupported and becomes a question.","clauses":[{"clause":"one dispute per transaction_id, each with its own amount and date","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 field 1 names 'the transaction being disputed' (singular), and fields 6 and 8 are that transaction's date and amount."},{"clause":"window from the earliest declined attempt to the current time","kind":"unsupported","source":"Doc 041 gives the suspicious period no bounds."}],"rewrite":{"id":"pin_lock_each_withdrawal","by":"model","do":"The customer may deny several successful transactions on the card, shown from the earliest declined PIN attempt (type 'atm_withdrawal_declined' or 'pos_declined') in get_transactions that led to the lock up to the current time from get_time, or any other recent successful transaction they say was not theirs. Doc 041 does not bound the suspicious period, so the customer's denial decides which are disputed. File one dispute per transaction_id, each with its own amount and date from get_transactions. Do not file one dispute for the total.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions","get_time"],"after":["from_pin_lock_handoff"],"if":"the PIN lock handoff has more than one successful transaction on the card that the customer denies","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"one dispute per transaction_id","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"file dispute for unauthorized transactions found","quote":"If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute, close card, order replacement.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"clause":"which transactions are denied","source":"none","why":"Doc 041 gives the suspicious period no bounds, so the customer says which successful transactions were not theirs."}]}},{"step":"greet","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the dispute purpose, and the identity values are the policy's verification set.","clauses":[]},{"step":"lookup_user","verdict":"valid","why":"The three user-lookup tool descriptions take a name, an email and a user id.","clauses":[]},{"step":"check_identity","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy states the 2-of-4 rule and the no-leak rule, and stopping after a repeated mismatch withholds access where no passage decides.","clauses":[{"clause":"if they still do not match, say you cannot verify them, and stop","kind":"kept","source":"Policy requires verification before any access and gives no retry or fallback rule, so the agent holds back access."}]},{"step":"get_time","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy guideline 4 states this.","clauses":[]},{"step":"log_verification","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy and the log_verification tool description state it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"one_dispute_at_a_time","verdict":"valid","why":"Each item is stated in doc 031 or policy, or derived from them.","clauses":[{"clause":"count each dispute filed earlier toward the open-dispute limit","kind":"derived","source":"(1) A dispute filed in this conversation is 'Dispute filed, investigation in progress' (doc 035 OPEN). (2) Doc 031 limits open disputes per account, so it counts toward that limit."},{"clause":"decide_card_action only after the last dispute","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes'."}]},{"step":"get_accounts","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 009 names the tool and its fields, and doc 005 assigns each product to a tier, which doc 031's tier limits use.","clauses":[{"clause":"tier from product name","kind":"derived","source":"(1) Doc 031 sets limits by 'checking account tier'. (2) Doc 005 lists which products belong to each tier."},{"clause":"class field is checking or savings, not tier","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 009 lists account_class, and the order_debit_card_5739 error 'is a {class} account' treats the class as checking or savings."}]},{"step":"get_cards","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 028 states the tool and the card_number_last_4 field.","clauses":[]},{"step":"get_transactions","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 1 names the tool.","clauses":[]},{"step":"match_failed","verdict":"valid","why":"A dispute needs a transaction ID found with the transactions tool, so a transaction missing from the records is not filed.","clauses":[{"clause":"never file a dispute for a transaction not in the records","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 field 1: the transaction ID comes from get_bank_account_transactions_9173."}]},{"step":"amount_differs_from_record","verdict":"valid","why":"The recorded amount and the incorrect_amount difference are derived from doc 031 fields 1 and 8, and whether to continue is asked.","clauses":[{"clause":"take the recorded amount for a whole-charge dispute","kind":"derived","source":"(1) Doc 031 field 1: the disputed transaction is the record. (2) Field 8: the amount being disputed. (3) When the whole charge is disputed, that amount is the recorded charge."},{"clause":"incorrect_amount uses the recorded charge minus the expected amount","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: incorrect_amount is 'Charged different amount than expected', and field 8 is the amount disputed, so the disputed part is the difference."},{"clause":"a dispute not filed sets no card action","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 performs the card action 'after filing all disputes'."}]},{"step":"pick_earliest_duplicate","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states it, and the one-charge amount follows from disputing a single transaction.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed amount is one charge","kind":"derived","source":"(1) Doc 031 says to dispute the earliest transaction. (2) Field 8 is the amount of that one transaction."}]},{"step":"get_dispute_status","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 states the tool.","clauses":[]},{"step":"count_open_disputes","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035's status descriptions separate investigations still in progress from resolved or closed ones.","clauses":[{"clause":"open vs not-open status sets","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035: OPEN, PENDING_DOCUMENTATION, UNDER_REVIEW and PROVISIONAL_CREDIT_ISSUED describe ongoing investigations. The RESOLVED_*, PROVISIONAL_REVERSED and CLOSED_NO_RESPONSE statuses describe finished ones."}]},{"step":"timeline_escalation","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 states the timelines and the escalation, doc 032 counts credit from filing, and asking before transferring withholds a transfer no passage forces.","clauses":[{"clause":"counted from filing_date","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 032: 'Must issue within 10 business days of dispute filing'. The doc 035 filing_date field supplies the date."},{"clause":"transfer only if the customer agrees","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 035 says 'escalate' without the manner, and policy says 'Do not transfer without asking the user first'."}]},{"step":"check_prefiling","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states each pre-filing rule, and doc 005 gives the tiers.","clauses":[{"clause":"tier from product name","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 tier limits plus the doc 005 tier product lists."}]},{"step":"explain_limit_and_choose","verdict":"valid","why":"The per-account limit and the 60-day rule are stated, and the choice among disputes is asked of the customer.","clauses":[{"clause":"rest can be filed once existing disputes close, while within 60 days","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 pre-filing rules 3 and 4 apply at the time of any later filing."}]},{"step":"gather_details","verdict":"valid","why":"Each question is a doc 031 field, a pre-filing item 6, or the doc 031 fraud split.","clauses":[]},{"step":"pin_compromised_unsure","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 11 defines each value.","clauses":[]},{"step":"type_from_customer_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 9 says 'Determine from user circumstances', and the step asks rather than guessing.","clauses":[]},{"step":"discovery_date_from_alert","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 7 and policy guideline 4 state it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"statement_date","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 counts the tiers from the statement, no tool returns statement dates, and the step asks the customer.","clauses":[{"clause":"statement reviewed at discovery is dated on or before discovery_date","kind":"derived","