e amount paid","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'Paid but never received item/service', and field 8 is the amount being disputed."}]},{"step":"p2p_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"card_present_fraud requires the physical card to be present and a P2P transfer does not use it, so with fraud suspected only card_not_present_fraud remains.","clauses":[{"clause":"P2P fraud is card_not_present_fraud","kind":"derived","source":"(1) Doc 031: card_present_fraud is 'Physical card used fraudulently... card was physically present'. (2) The only other fraud category is card_not_present_fraud. (3) A P2P transfer is not physical use of the card, and the customer is asked if they report physical use."}]},{"step":"in_person_fraud_with_card_held","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 sends in-store/physical transactions with suspected fraud to card_present_fraud, and field 11 defines yes_observed and unknown.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recurring_charge_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"Docs 031 and 034 state the category, the mapping and the block order, doc 032 states that credit is not required, and the closed-card advice is doc 025's.","clauses":[{"clause":"if the card is being closed, tell them to update recurring payments","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 025 closing step 6: 'Any recurring payments linked to this card will need to be updated'. The set_debit_card_recurring_block_7382 tool requires an ACTIVE card."}]},{"step":"lost_card_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The doc 031 categories, the doc 025 reasons and the doc 030 trigger support each clause.","clauses":[{"clause":"close reason lost or stolen","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 025 lists lost and stolen as reasons, and the customer has reported the card as such."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_journal","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"rho_atm_amount_check","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 takes the journal from the transactions, and the confirmed-discrepancy amount is arithmetic on the record and the customer's claim.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount = recorded withdrawal − cash received","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: atm_cash_discrepancy is 'ATM dispensed wrong amount', and field 8 is the amount disputed, which is the undispensed difference."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_not_validated","verdict":"rewrite","why":"Leaving disputed_amount open blocks a required argument, but doc 031 field 8 and the category definition give it as the amount the customer says was not dispensed, confirmed with them.","clauses":[{"clause":"the documents do not say which amount to dispute","kind":"unsupported","source":"Doc 031 field 8 ('The dollar amount being disputed') and atm_cash_discrepancy ('dispensed wrong amount or no cash') decide it: the cash the customer says was not dispensed."},{"clause":"do not file if the customer accepts the record or skips","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 033 says the customer 'may still file' but does not require filing."}],"rewrite":{"id":"rho_atm_not_validated","by":"model","do":"If the customer accepts the record or asks to skip this dispute, do not file it. Tell them it was not filed and go on to their next dispute; it sets no card action. If they still want a formal dispute, file it as atm_cash_discrepancy with transaction_type atm_withdrawal and card_action keep_active. The disputed_amount is the cash they say the machine failed to dispense (the amount they say they requested minus the cash received). Confirm that figure with the customer before filing.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["rho_atm_amount_check","get_transactions","gather_details"],"after":["rho_atm_amount_check"],"if":"a Rho-Bank ATM record shows the amount dispensed equal to the cash the customer received (claim not validated)","quote":"If journal shows correct amount dispensed, inform customer the claim cannot be validated but they may still file a formal dispute","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033","basis":[{"clause":"may still file a formal dispute","quote":"If journal shows correct amount dispensed, inform customer the claim cannot be validated but they may still file a formal dispute","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"clause":"ATM cash discrepancy category","quote":"'atm_cash_discrepancy': ATM dispensed wrong amount or no cash","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"disputed amount is the amount the customer disputes","quote":"The dollar amount being disputed.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"keep_active","quote":"'atm_cash_discrepancy' → 'keep_active'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"confirm the figure with the customer","source":"none","why":"The record does not show the requested amount, so the customer is asked to confirm the amount they dispute."}]}},{"step":"atm_deposit_images","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 and the tool description state it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"deposit_compare","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states the comparison, and not filing when the customer accepts the records withholds a write that no passage forces.","clauses":[{"clause":"do not file if the customer accepts the records","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 033 gives no rule on filing after the comparison."}]},{"step":"third_party_atm_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 third-party items 1-3 state it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"atm_affidavit_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recommend_police_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 13 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"police_report_incident_total","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 036 recommends a police report for suspected fraud at any amount, and police_report_filed is a required boolean on each filing.","clauses":[{"clause":"ask and recommend when the incident total exceeds $500","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 036: 'For suspected fraud, we recommend also filing a police report, especially for amounts over $500'. The tool requires police_report_filed."}]},{"step":"police_report_question_under_500","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 036 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 field 14 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement_reuse","verdict":"valid","why":"The customer's agreement that this conversation is their statement covers every dispute described in it.","clauses":[{"clause":"do not ask again; pass true","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 field 14: 'Set to true if the customer agrees'. The agreement was already given in this conversation."}]},{"step":"decide_provisional_credit","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 032 states the REQUIRED and NOT REQUIRED items and doc 033 states the ATM cases; setting false where credit is discretionary withholds an offer that no passage mandates.","clauses":[{"clause":"passing the 60-day age rule means within 60 days of the statement","kind":"derived","source":"(1) The statement is dated on or after the transaction. (2) So now − statement ≤ now − transaction ≤ 60 days."},{"clause":"unauthorized_transaction counts as non-fraud for the merchant-contact item","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'use only when fraud is NOT suspected'. Doc 032 item 2 applies to 'non-fraud disputes'."},{"clause":"third-party ATM cash discrepancy not set false by merchant contact","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 033 names third-party ATM disputes: 'Provisional credit is still required within 10 business days'."},{"clause":"set false where a NOT REQUIRED item applies","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 032 says 'may be offered at discretion' without deciding when, so the offer is held back."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_confirmed_provisional","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 names the confirmed Rho-Bank discrepancy and says credit is issued immediately, and keeping doc 032's other conditions withholds credit where 033 speaks only to timing.","clauses":[{"clause":"merchant contact does not apply","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 033 names this 